      "transition": "fade",
      "narration": "Every routing engine, from Google Maps to OSPF inside your datacenter's routers, has to answer one deceptively simple question: what is the cheapest way to get from here to there? Dijkstra's algorithm, published in 1959, is the workhorse that answers it for graphs with non-negative edge weights. In this video we'll rebuild it from the ground up — the greedy insight, why it's provably correct, and where it quietly falls apart.",
