          "data": {
            "title": "The two guarantees underneath",
            "items": [
              "Optimal substructure — a shortest path's every prefix is itself a shortest path",
              "Relaxation is monotone — dist[v] only ever decreases, never increases",
              "Invariant — once a node is settled, dist[v] equals its true shortest distance",
              "Non-negative weights — required so a settled distance can never later shrink",
              "Bellman-Ford relaxes all edges V-1 times; Dijkstra relaxes each edge exactly once"
